          "question": "What is described as first-line treatment for newly diagnosed high blood pressure?",
          "answer": "The first-line treatment for newly diagnosed high blood pressure (hypertension) typically includes lifestyle modifications and medication. Lifestyle changes may focus on dietary adjustments (such as the DASH diet), increased physical activity, weight loss if overweight, and moderation of alcohol intake. \n\nFor pharmacological treatment, commonly prescribed classes of medication include thiazide diuretics, ACE inhibitors, angiotensin II receptor blockers (ARBs), and calcium channel blockers. A healthcare provider will consider individual patient factors when choosing the specific treatment.\n\nI could not cover details about specific medications, dosages, or guidelines specific to particular populations (like those with certain comorbidities).\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
